\p
\v 10 Then Shemuel¦128655 \add ≈passed on everything that Yahweh¦128660 had said\add* to the people¦128663 who were requesting a king from him,
\v 11 telling them, “\add ≈If¦128677 you all have a king¦128673 reigning¦128675 over you, this is what he'll demand\add*: he will \add ≈conscript\add* your sons¦128679 and appoint¦128681 them \add ≈as his cavalry or charioteers, or they'll run¦128685 as foot-soldiers in¦128683 front¦128686\add*, of his chariot¦128687.
\v 12 \add ≈Others he'll appoint¦128689 a commander of various units\add*. \add ≈Some will end up ploughing his fields or harvesting¦128698 his crops, or manufacturing his weapons¦128700 and¦128689 chariots¦128704\add*.
\v 13 He'll take¦128709 your¦128708 daughters¦128708 to \add ≈manufacture perfumes¦128710\add*, or to be cooks¦128711 and¦128706 bakers¦128712.
\v 14 He'll confiscate your \add ≈best\add* fields¦128716 and vineyards¦128719 and olive¦128720 orchards¦128720, and give to his servants¦128724 \add to control\add*.
\v 15 Then¦128726 he'll demand a tenth of your seeds¦128726 and \add ≈grape harvests for\add* his officials¦128730 and his servants¦128731.
\v 16 He'll commandeer \add some of\add* your \add ≈best\add* male and female¦128738 servants and young¦128741 men¦128741, and he'll impound \add some of\add* your donkeys¦128745, then¦128733 he'll use \add them all\add* for his \add ≈projects\add*.
\v 17 He'll \add ≈expect\add* a tenth of your \add ≈sheep and goats\add*, and you yourselves \add ≈will end up being\add* his slaves.
\v 18 \add ≈When¦128770 that all happens\add*, you'll all cry¦128758 out \add ≈in front\add* of the king¦128762 who you chose¦128764 for yourselves, \add ≈but¦128758\add* Yahweh¦128769 won't¦128766 be answering¦128768 you \add ≈at that time\add*.”
\rem /s1 Israel's Request for a King Granted
\p
\v 19 \add ≈However,\add* the people¦128775 refused¦128774 to \add ≈consider Shemuel's advice\add* and¦128779 they¦128779 \add ≈argued\add*, “No, \add ≈we want\add* a king¦128784 over us
\v 20 \add ≈so\add* we'll be like all the other nations¦128794. Our¦128800 king¦128796 will judge¦128795 us, and¦128788 will \add ≈lead out our warriors in battle¦128802\add*.”
\v 21 Shemuel¦128805 listened¦128804 to \add ≈everything the people¦128810 said, and¦128811 passed it on¦128812 to\add* Yahweh¦128813,
\v 22 and Yahweh¦128817 told \add *him\add*, “\add ≈Do what they're asking and get them\add* a king¦128825.” \add ≈So\add* Shemuel¦128820 \add told the people¦128830 and then sent them all back to their¦128822 homes\add*.
\c 9
\s1 Sha'ul is chosen as king
