\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* there was a Benyamite man named Kish¦128846 (son of Abiel¦128849, son of Zeror¦128852, son of Bekorath, son of Afiah¦128858, the son of a Yaminite¦128862 man) \add ≈who was strong and wealthy¦128864\add*.
\v 2 \add @Kish\add* had a son \add ≈named\add* Sha'ul¦128871 who was a handsome¦128873 young¦128872 man and good—\add ≈in fact there¦128874 wasn't any Israeli¦128877 man\add* better than him, \add and\add* he was \add ≈head and shoulders¦128880 taller than anyone else\add*.
\p
\v 3 \add ≈One time,\add* the female donkeys of Sha'uls father¦128890 Kish \add ≈had gone missing\add*, and Kish \add ≈told\add* his son, “Take one of the servants¦128905 with you¦128901, and \add ≈pack up\add* and go¦128907 and find those donkeys.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦128913\add* \add #they\add* passed through the Efrayimite hill country¦128914, then¦128913 through the Shalishah¦128920 \add ≈region\add*, but they didn't find them. Then¦128913 they went through the Shaalim¦128926 \add ≈region\add*, but there¦128927 was nothing, \add ≈so\add* \add #they\add* \add ≈continued on¦128914\add* through the land of the Benyamites, but they didn't find them.
\v 5 \add Finally,\add* they¦128936 entered the Tsuf \add ≈area\add*, and \add eventually\add* Sha'ul¦128939 said¦128940 to his servant¦128941, “Come on. Let's \add ≈go¦128946 back home in case\add* my father¦128950 \add ≈stops worrying\add* about the donkeys¦128953 and \add starts\add* worrying about us.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈But¦128957\add* he \add ≈replied\add*, “Listen, please¦128961. There's an honoured¦128968 man of God¦128964 in¦128965 this city¦128965. \add ≈Everything he says comes¦128974 true\add*. Let's go there¦128977 now. Perhaps he'll tell us \add ≈which¦128984 way we should¦128976 have gone\add*.”
\p
\v 7 “\add ≈Okay, then¦128989.\add* We can go \add there¦129003\add*,” Sha'ul¦128990 \add ≈responded¦128989\add*, “but¦128989 what \add ≈can we give\add* the man? \add ≈We don't¦129003 have any more food¦128999 in our bags, and¦128989 we never brought along a gift¦129002. What else do we have?\add*”
\p
\v 8 “Look,” answered¦129013 the servant¦129012, “I've got a \add ≈small silver¦129023 coin\add*. We can give¦129024 that to the man¦129025 and¦129011 he'll tell us where to go.”
\v 9 (In Yisrael¦129035 before then, \add ≈when people wanted an answer from\add* God¦129042, they'd say, “Come and¦129044 let us go¦129044 to the ‘seer’,” because¦129048 the prophet¦129049 of today was called¦129051 the ‘seer’ before.)
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈Good idea\add*,” Sha'ul¦129056 told his servant¦129057. “Let's go¦129062 then¦129055.” \add ≈So¦129055\add* they¦129063 went¦129063 to the city¦129066 there¦129069 where¦129067 the man¦129070 of God¦129071 was.
\v 11 They were \add ≈climbing up the rise towards\add* the city¦129076 \add ≈when\add* they \add ≈met some\add* young¦129079 women¦129079 going¦129074 out to draw water¦129082, and they \add ≈asked\add* them, “Is the seer in¦129075 \add ≈town¦129076\add*?”
\v 12 “\add ≈Yes he is\add*,” they answered¦129089. “Hurry \add ≈though\add*, because¦129098 he's come¦129100 to the city¦129101 today \add to offer\add* the sacrifice¦129103 for the people¦129105 at¦129106 the high¦129106 place¦129106.
\v 13 You'll find him as soon as you enter¦129108 the city¦129109, before¦129113 he goes up to the high place¦129115 to eat. The people¦129121 won't¦129118 eat until¦129122 he \add ≈gets there\add*, because¦129117 he himself will bless¦129128 the sacrifice¦129129. Afterwards, \add ≈those¦129134 who've been invited¦129134\add* will eat \add together there\add*. So go up there now \add ≈and you'll soon find him\add*.”
\v 14 \add ≈So¦129144\add* they went on up into the city, and¦129144 as they were entering, wow, there was Shemuel¦129151 \add ≈coming out towards¦129153\add* them to go up to the high place¦129155.
\p
\v 15 \add ≈On¦129169 the previous day¦129164,\add* Yahweh¦129158 \add ≈had quietly told\add* Shemuel¦129163,
\v 16 “About¦129172 this time tomorrow¦129174, I'll¦129175 send a Benyamite man¦129177 to you, and you should anoint¦129180 him to be ruler¦129181 over my people Yisrael¦129185. He will \add ≈rescue¦129186\add* my people from the Philistines¦129191, because I've¦129193 \add ≈noticed\add* my people because \add ≈I heard their¦129199 cries\add*.”
\p
\v 17 Then¦129202 Shemuel saw¦129203 Sha'ul¦129206, and¦129207 Yahweh¦129207 told him¦129208, “Look, \add that's\add* the man¦129210 that I you¦129213 \add about\add*. \add ≈He\add* will \add help control\add* my people¦129216.”
\v 18 \add ≈As\add* Sha'ul¦129219 approached¦129218 Shemuel¦129222 \add ≈right there in the middle¦129223 of the city gateway\add*, he \add ≈asked¦129225\add*, “Please tell me, where's¦129230 the seer's¦129234 house¦129233?”
\p
\v 19 “I am the seer,” Shemuel¦129237 answered¦129236, “\add Now,\add* Go up to the high¦129246 place¦129246 \add ≈ahead of me\add*, and¦129236 you'll eat¦129247 with¦129251 me today. In the morning¦129251, I'll tell you \add ≈what you want to know\add*, then¦129236 I'll send¦129250 you off.
\v 20 As for your donkeys¦129258 that¦129259 were lost three¦129262 days¦129263 ago, don't¦129264 \add ≈worry anymore about them\add* because¦129271 they've¦129272 been found¦129272. Now, all of Yisrael¦129277 is wanting your father's \add ≈household¦129281\add*, and¦129258 \add ≡wanting\add* you \add in particular\add*.”
\v 21 “\add ≈But¦129285\add* I'm a Benyamite,” Sha'ul¦129286 responded¦129285, “\add That's\add* the smallest¦129293 tribe in Yisrael¦129296, and my clan's the lowliest¦129298 of all the Benyamite clans¦129301. \add ≈So\add* why \add ≈did you¦129305 talk to me like that\add*?”
\p
\v 22 Then Shemuel took¦129311 Sha'ul¦129315 and his servant¦129318 to the room¦129323 \add where the meal had been prepared\add*, and he gave¦129321 them a place¦129323 at¦129324 the head¦129324 of \add ≈table—even above the invited¦129325 guests\add*. (There were about¦129327 thirty¦129327 men.)
\v 23 And Shemuel¦129331 told the cook, “Give the \add special\add* \add ≈piece of meat\add* that¦129337 I \add ≈showed\add* you and¦129330 said to keep aside.”
\v 24 \add ≈So¦129347\add* the cook lifted¦129347 the \add ≈cooked leg\add* and¦129347 \add ≈placed it in front¦129355\add* of Sha'ul. Then¦129347 \add &Shemuel¦129377\add* told \add Sha'ul\add*, “Look, \add ≈this has been reserved for you\add*. Eat \add <it\add*, because¦129364 it's been kept¦129366 \add ≈until\add* the appointed¦129365 time¦129365 \add ≈when I could call these people¦129370 together\add*.”
\s1 Shemuel anoints Sha'ul with oil
\s4 Full kingdom
\p \add ≈So\add* Sha'ul ate¦129373 with Shemuel that¦129359 day¦129378,
\v 25 and then¦129381 they¦129381 went¦129381 \add back\add* from the high¦129382 place¦129382 down into the city¦129383, and \add @Shemuel\add* spoke¦129384 with Sha'ul¦129387 on \add his house\add* roof¦129390.
\p
\v 26 They rose early¦129392 \add the next day\add*. At dawn, Shemuel¦129397 had called¦129396 to Sha'ul on the roof¦129401, saying, “Get up and I will send¦129405 you¦129405 \add ≈off\add*.” \add ≈So¦129392\add* Sha'ul got up, and the two of them went¦129408 outside¦129412.
\rem /s1 Samuel Anoints Saul as Ruler; Samuel Anoints Saul
\v 27 \add When\add* they \add ≈reached\add* the edge of the city¦129417, Shemuel said¦129419 to Sha'ul¦129422, “\add ≈Tell your servant¦129424 to go¦129425 on ahead\add*,” and \add so\add* he went¦129427 on ahead. “But¦129418 you stand \add ≈here\add*, and I'll \add ≈give you the message¦129434 from\add* God¦129435.”
\c 10
\rem /s1 Samuel Anoints Saul as King
\p
\v 1 Then Shemuel¦129439 took¦129438 a flask¦129442 of oil¦129443, and poured¦129444 it on \add @Sha'ul's\add* head¦129447 and kissed¦129448 him, and told him, “It's Yahweh¦129454 who has anointed¦129453 you to be ruler¦129458 over his \add ≈chosen people\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈After you leave me today\add* \add and get back to\add* Benyamite territory¦129470, then you'll \add ≈see\add* two men¦129465 near Rachel's¦129469 tomb in¦129470 Tseltsah, and they'll say to you, ‘The donkeys that¦129477 you went¦129478 to look for have been found¦129475. \add ≈But¦129463\add*, wow, your father has stopped worrying¦129487 about the donkeys and \add now\add* he's worried about \em you\em* \add ≈and trying to figure out what he should do¦129491\add*.’
\v 3 Then¦129494 further¦129496 on from there, \add ≈as you approach\add* the oak tree¦129500 at Tabor¦129501, you'll find three men¦129505 going¦129506 to Beyt-El to worship God¦129509. One¦129510 will be taking three young goats, one will be carrying three rounds¦129521 loaves¦129521 of bread¦129522, and¦129494 one will be carrying a wine in a container.
\v 4 They'll ask¦129529 about \add ≈how you're doing\add* and¦129529 give¦129532 you two¦129534 loaves of bread¦129536 which you should accept¦129537.
\v 5 After¦129540 that, you'll come to the hill of God¦129544 (where¦129545 there's a camp of Philistine \add warriors\add*). \add ≈When you enter\add* the town¦129553, you'll meet a group of prophets¦129556 descending from the \add ≈altar area\add*,
\v 6 and Yahweh's¦129570 spirit¦129569 will rush onto you. Then¦129567 you'll \add join\add* them in prophesying¦129571, and you'll be transformed into a different person¦129574.
\v 7 \add ≈When¦129577 this all comes true\add*, do¦129584 whatever you think is correct because¦129578 God¦129590 \add ≈will be helping\add* you.
\v 8 Then¦129593 go¦129593 \add ≈ahead of me\add* to Gilgal¦129595 and wait \add there\add* for seven¦129605 days¦129606, until¦129608 I get there and tell you what to do. I'll¦129612 join you to offer burnt¦129601 offerings \add and\add* to sacrifice¦129602 peace¦129604 offerings.
\rem /s1 Saul Prophesies; Saul Made King; Samuel's Signs Are Fulfilled
\p
\v 9 Then as Sha'ul \add ≈started to leave\add* Shemuel, God¦129627 \add ≈changed¦129624 his thinking\add*. Then all Shemuel's predictions came¦129630 true that day¦129635,
\v 10 \add ≈so when\add* \add @Sha'ul and his servant\add* came¦129639 to the hill, a group of prophets met \add #them\add* and God's¦129641 spirit¦129649 rushed¦129647 onto \add @Sha'ul\add* and he \add ≈joined them in¦129652\add* prophesying.
\v 11 Then¦129654 everyone¦129655 who had known \add @Sha'ul\add* \add ≈previously\add* heard him¦129657 prophesying with¦129681 the prophets, \add ≈they¦129660 asked each other\add*, “What's happened¦129675 to Kish's¦129678 son? Is Sha'ul really a prophet \add now\add*?”
\v 12 A man¦129684 from there¦129685 answered¦129683, “And who is \em their¦129688\em* father¦129688?” So¦129683 after that it became¦129692 a common saying, “Has Sha'ul¦129695 also \add ≈become a prophet¦129696\add*?”\x + \xo 10:12: \xt 1Sam 19:23-24.\x*
\v 13 When¦129698 he had finished prophesying¦129699, he ascended to the \add ≈altar area\add*.
\p
\v 14 \add Later,\add* Sha'ul's¦129705 uncle¦129704 asked him and¦129703 his servant¦129709, “Where did¦129711 you¦129711 \add two\add* \add ≈take off to\add*?”
\p “To look¦129713 for the donkeys¦129716,” Sha'ul replied. “\add ≈But¦129703 we couldn't find them, so\add* we went¦129721 to Shemuel¦129724.”
\p
\v 15 “\add ≈And what did¦129735 he tell you?\add*” \add *the\add* uncle¦129727 \add ≈asked\add*.
\p
\v 16 “He \add ≈assured\add* us that the donkeys¦129749 had been found¦129748,” Sha'ul¦129740 replied. \add ≈But¦129739\add* he didn't¦129754 tell him anything that Shemuel¦129760 had said \add ≈about becoming king\add*.
\s1 Sha'ul is selected as king
\rem /s1 Saul Proclaimed King; Saul Is Acclaimed King; Saul Is Acclaimed as King
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 17 Then Shemuel¦129764 summoned¦129763 the people¦129767 \add to come before\add* Yahweh¦129770 at Mitspah,
\v 18 and he told \add *them\add*, “Yahweh¦129783, the god¦129784 of Yisrael, says¦129782, ‘I myself brought¦129787 Yisrael out of Egypt¦129791. I rescued you from \add ≈Egyptian control\add*, and from all the kingdoms¦129799 that¦129800 oppressed¦129800 you.’
\v 19 \add ≈But¦129803 since then¦129803\add*, you all have rejected¦129805 your god¦129808—the one who saves you from all your calamities¦129816 and distresses¦129817. And you've all said¦129818 to him, ‘\add ≈We'd rather have\add* a king¦129822 over us.’ \add ≈So¦129803\add* station yourselves¦129826 now \add ≈in front¦129827\add* of Yahweh¦129828 by your tribes¦129829 and \add ≈clans¦129830\add*.”
\p
\v 20 Then¦129832 Shemuel¦129833 had all the Israeli¦129838 tribes approach, and¦129839 the tribe of Benyamin¦129841 was selected.
\v 21 Then he had all the Benyamite clans approach, and the Matri¦129852 clan was selected. Then Kish's¦129857 son, Sha'ul¦129854 was selected and they tried to find him, but¦129843 \add ≈they couldn't find him anywhere\add*
\v 22 \add ≈so\add* they¦129862 asked Yahweh again¦129864, “\add ≈Is that man¦129869 around here anywhere\add*?”
\p “Look, he's hiding¦129876 among the supplies,” Yahweh \add ≈replied\add*.
\p
\v 23 \add ≈So¦129881\add* they ran and got him from there¦129883, and \add when\add* he took his place among the people, he was head and shoulders¦129891 taller¦129887 than anyone else.
\v 24 Then¦129894 Shemuel \add ≈announced to everyone¦129900\add*, “Can you see the one that Yahweh¦129906 has chosen¦129903? Certainly there's¦129908 no one else like him among all the people.”
\p All the people saw \add <that\add* and¦129894 \add ≈responded¦129894\add*, “\add ≈Long\add* live the king¦129919.”
\p
\v 25 Then Shemuel¦129923 \add ≈explained\add* how the kingship¦129929 would work, and wrote¦129930 it in a book and placed¦129932 it \add ≈in front¦129933\add* of Yahweh¦129934. Then \add *he\add* sent¦129935 \add ≈everyone¦129926 home¦129943\add*.
\v 26 Shemuel¦129947 also went \add ≈home¦129949\add* to Gibeah¦129950, \add ≈accompanied by some of\add* the powerful \add ≈warriors¦129953\add* whose¦129958 hearts¦129958 God¦129957 had touched¦129956.
\v 27 \add ≈But¦129960 some worthless¦129961 men asked\add*, “How can that one save¦129965 us?” and they despised¦129967 \add @Sha'ul\add* and didn't¦129968 bring him¦129967 any gifts, but¦129960 he \add ≈made no comment\add*.
\c 11
\s1 Sha'ul rescues Yabesh from the Ammonites
\rem /s1 Saul Rescues the City of Jabesh; Saul Defeats the Ammonites
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add About a month later,\add*\f + \fr 11:1 \ft This appears only in a few ancient documents.\f* Nahash¦129978 the Ammonite¦129979 \add took his men¦129988\add* and camped \add ≈around\add* Yabesh-Gilead¦129984, and the \add ≈leaders\add* of Yabesh told \add *him\add*, “\add ≈Make a treaty with\add* us, and we'll serve¦129997 you¦129997.”
\p
\v 2 “\add Yes¦130002,\add* I'll¦130004 \add ≈make an treaty with¦130003\add* you,” Nahash¦130001 \add ≈replied\add*, “by gouging¦130006 out \add ≈all of your\add* right¦130011 \add #eyes\add* \add ≈in¦130003 order to shame\add* all Yisrael¦130018.”
\p
\v 3 “\add Oh! Then¦130020\add* leave us alone for seven¦130026 days¦130027,” the Yabesh¦130023 elders¦130022 \add ≈responded¦130020\add*, “so that we can send¦130028 messengers¦130029 through all the territory¦130031 of Yisrael¦130032. If no one \add ≈will come¦130038 to rescue\add* us, then¦130020 we'll \add ≈surrender¦130038\add* to you¦130039.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈When¦130053\add* the messengers¦130042 arrived \add ≈where Sha'ul¦130044 lived\add* at¦130047 Gibeah¦130043 and¦130041 \add ≈passed the news onto the people\add*, \add ≈everyone¦130048 started wailing loudly\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈At that time\add*, Sha'ul¦130059 was walking home behind the cattle¦130062 and¦130058 \add *he\add* asked, “What's with \add all\add* the people¦130070 wailing?” Then¦130058 they¦130072 \add ≈told\add* him \add ≈what the messengers from Yabesh¦130080 had said¦130066\add*.
\v 6 God's¦130091 spirit¦130083 rushed¦130082 on¦130089 Sha'ul¦130088 as he heard¦130089 the message¦130093, and¦130082 \add ≈he became very angry\add*.
\v 7 Then he took¦130099 a pair of cattle and \add ≈chopped\add* them into pieces¦130102, and sent¦130103 messengers¦130109 to take them \add ≈throughout\add* Yisrael¦130107 and \add ≈announce\add*, “This is what will be done¦130120 to the cattle of \add ≈anyone¦130131 who doesn't join\add* Sha'ul¦130116 and Shemuel \add in¦130108 battle\add*.”
\p Then Yahweh¦130125 \add ≈caused the people¦130128 to be afraid of him\add*, and they united together.
\v 8 \add ≈When¦130133\add* \add @Sha'ul\add* assembled them at¦130134 Bezek¦130134, there were three¦130139 hundred¦130140 thousand \add warriors¦130142\add* from Yisrael¦130138 and¦130133 thirty¦130144 thousand from Yehudah¦130143,
\v 9 and they told the \add original\add* messengers, “\add Go and\add* \add ≈tell the leaders\add* of Yabesh¦130167-Gilead, ‘Tomorrow you'll all \add ≈be rescued\add* \add ≈by the time that\add* the sun's \add ≈at¦130160 its hottest\add*.’ ”
\v 10 \add ≈So¦130170\add* the Yabesh¦130172 \add ≈leaders told\add* \add Nahash\add*, “\add ≈We'll surrender\add* to you all tomorrow¦130173, then¦130170 you can do¦130176 to us \add ≈whatever¦130178 seems good¦130180 to you all\add*.”
\p
\v 11 The next day, Sha'ul¦130187 divided \add &his\add* warriors into three¦130191 divisions, and they \add ≈attacked the Ammonite camp¦130196 before the sun rose\add*. Then they \add ≈slaughtered the Ammonites¦130202\add* until¦130203 the hottest part of the day. \add &Their\add* remaining¦130211 warriors were scattered¦130209 \add ≈so completely that no two of them were able to stay\add* together¦130215.
\s1 Sha'ul reaffirmed as king
\rem /s1 Saul Confirmed as King
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 12 Then¦130217 the people¦130218 \add ≈asked\add* Shemuel¦130221, “Who \add ≈were the ones saying that Sha'ul¦130224 wasn't fit to\add* reign¦130225 over us? \add ≈Bring them here\add* and¦130229 we'll \add ≈execute\add* them.”
\p
\v 13 “\add ≈No one's going to be executed\add* today,” Sha'ul¦130232 said¦130231, “because¦130239 today Yahweh¦130243 has \add ≈rescued\add* Yisrael¦130245.”
\p
\v 14 “Come \add on then\add*,” said¦130248 Shemuel¦130249. “Let's go¦130254 to Gilgal¦130255 and renew¦130256 the kingship there¦130257.”
\v 15 \add ≈So¦130260\add* all the people when to Gilgal¦130264 and \add ≈in¦130272 front¦130270\add* of Yahweh they \add ≈reaffirmed Sha'ul as king¦130265\add*. Then¦130260 they offered sacrifices¦130273 \add as\add* peace¦130277 offerings¦130277 \add ≈to\add* Yahweh, then¦130260 Sha'ul and the people \add ≈celebrated together\add*.
\c 12
