\v 8 After¦130439 Yacob¦130442 went to Egypt and your ancestors cried¦130444 out to Yahweh, then Yahweh sent Mosheh¦130453 and Aharon¦130456, and they brought¦130457 your ancestors out of Egypt and settled¦130462 them into this place¦130463.\x + \xo 12:8: \xt Exo 2:23.\x*
\v 9 Then they forgot¦130466 their¦130470 god¦130470 Yahweh¦130469, and he \add ≈allowed them to be oppressed by\add* Sisera¦130474 (the commander¦130475 of the army from Hazor¦130478), and the Philistines¦130481, and the king¦130483 of Moab¦130484. Then they fought¦130485 against¦130486 them\x + \xo 12:9: a \xt Jdg 4:2; \xo b \xt Jdg 13:1; \xo c \xt Jdg 3:12.\x*
\v 10 and cried¦130488 out to Yahweh, ‘We have sinned¦130495, because¦130496 we've abandoned¦130497 Yahweh and have served¦130501 the Baals¦130504 and the Ashtorets¦130507. \add ≈But¦130488 if\add* you rescue¦130509 us now from our enemies¦130511, we will serve¦130512 you.’\x + \xo 12:10: \xt Jdg 10:10-15.\x*
