\p
\v 3 Then¦130871 Yonatan \add ≈attacked¦130871 and defeated¦130871\add* the Philistine unit that¦130876 was at¦130877 Geba¦130877, and the Philistines¦130875 heard¦130878 \add about it\add*. \add ≈So¦130871\add* Sha'ul¦130880 \add had\add* a trumpet¦130882 blown \add ≈throughout\add* the \add ≈country, with¦130877 the message\add*, “\add ≈Listen all you\add* Hebrews¦130888.”
\v 4 All of Yisrael heard¦130893 \add ≈the news that\add* Sha'ul had \add ≈wiped out\add* a Philistine outpost, and¦130890 \add realised that\add* Yisrael had become \add ≈repulsive to\add* the Philistines¦130900. \add ≈So¦130890\add* the people¦130907 were \add ≈summoned¦130906 to join\add* Sha'ul at¦130905 Gilgal¦130910.
\p
\v 5 The Philistines¦130912 \add ≈assembled themselves\add* to fight¦130915 Yisrael¦130918 \add with¦130936\add* thirty¦130919 thousand chariots¦130921, six¦130922 thousand mounted cavalry, and warriors \add ≈as numerous\add* as the sand on¦130936 the \add ≈beach\add*. They went¦130934 to Mikmas and camped¦130935 \add there\add*, east of Beyt-Aven.
\v 6 \add ≈But¦130941\add* the \add ≈Israeli¦130942 warriors¦130941\add* were \add ≈very anxious\add* because¦130944 their troops¦130950 were \add ≈so outnumbered\add*, \add ≈so\add* they¦130943 hid¦130951 in caves¦130953 and thickets¦130954, among rocks¦130955, and in tombs¦130956 and wells.
\v 7 \add ≈Some of them\add* crossed the Yordan¦130963 \add River\add* to the Gad¦130965 and¦130959 Gilead¦130966 regions¦130964.
