\v 12 then¦131038 I \add ≈thought\add*, ‘The Philistines¦131041 \add ≈are about to attack us at\add* Gilgal¦131043, and I haven't \add ≈offered any gift to\add* Yahweh¦131045.’ So¦131038 I forced¦131048 myself¦131048, and offered up the burnt¦131050 up offering¦131050.”
\p
\v 13 “\add ≈That was stupid of you\add*,” Shemuel¦131054 \add ≈responded¦131053\add*. “You haven't \add ≈obeyed what your god¦131065 Yahweh instructed¦131067\add*, because¦131068 \add if you had,\add* then Yahweh would have established¦131070 your reign over Yisrael¦131077 \add ≈forever¦131080\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈But¦131082\add* now your kingdom¦131083 won't¦131084 \add ≈survive\add*. Yahweh¦131088 has found a man who's \add ≈loyal to him\add* and¦131082 \add *he's\add* commanded¦131104 \add @that man\add* to lead his people¦131097, because¦131098 you haven't \add ≈obeyed\add* him.\x + \xo 13:14: \xt Acts 13:22.\x*
