\p
\v 39 \add ≈When¦139139\add* David¦139140 heard that Nabal had died¦139142, he said¦139144, “Blessed be Yahweh, who has \add ≈judged\add* the case of \add ≈Nabal's¦139143 insult\add* and¦139139 has \add ≈prevented\add* his servant¦139157 from \add ≈doing the wrong thing\add*. And Yahweh has \add ≈repaid Nabal for his own evil\add*.”
\p Then¦139139 David sent¦139166 \add messengers\add* to Abigail¦139169 \add ≈about\add* taking her as a wife.
\v 40 \add *His\add* servants¦139175 went¦139174 to \add *her\add* at Carmel¦139180 and¦139174 told her, “David¦139176 sent¦139185 us to take¦139187 you \add back\add* to become his wife.”
\p
\v 41 She \add ≈knelt down with her face¦139193 to the ground¦139194 and¦139191 replied\add*, “See, your¦139197 female servant¦139197 is \add ready\add* for washing the feet¦139200 of my master's¦139202 servants¦139201 like a slave¦139198 woman.”
\v 42 Then¦139204 Abigail¦139206 and five¦139211 of her¦139214 servant girls quickly¦139204 \add ≈got ready\add*, and she mounted the donkey¦139210. She followed the messengers¦139217 to \add ≈where David¦139218 was\add* and became¦139219 a wife for him.
\p
\v 43 David¦139228 had also married Ahinoam¦139226 from Yizre'el¦139229, \add ≈so\add* both of them became¦139230 his wives¦139235.
\v 44 (\add ≈Meanwhile\add* Sha'ul¦139238 had given¦139239 his daughter¦139243, David' wife¦139244 Mikal, to Palti¦139246, Layish's¦139249 son from Gallim¦139251.)\x + \xo 25:44: \xt 2Sam 3:14-16.\x*
\c 26
\s1 David spares Sha'ul again
\rem /s1 David Spares Saul Again; David Spares Saul's Life Again; David Again Spares Saul's Life; David Spares Saul's Life a Second Time
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add One time some\add* Zifites¦139254 went¦139253 to Sha'ul¦139257 at¦139263 Gibeah¦139258 and¦139253 told \add <him\add*, “Isn't David¦139261 hiding¦139262 himself¦139262 on¦139263 the Hakilah¦139264 hill \add ≈opposite\add* Yeshimon¦139267?”\x + \xo 26:1: \xt Psa 54 header.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈So¦139269\add* Sha'ul¦139270 got ready with¦139288 three¦139278 thousand¦139280 chosen¦139282 Israeli¦139282 warriors and¦139269 went to the Zif¦139276 wilderness to search¦139284 for David¦139287.
\v 3 \add *They\add* camped at¦139294 Hakilah¦139295 hill (\add ≈opposite\add* Yeshimon¦139300) by the path¦139303, \add ≈but¦139292\add* David¦139304 stayed in¦139294 the wilderness \add ≈when\add* he saw the Sha'ul¦139293 was \add ≈there trying to get\add* him.
\v 4 (\add *He'd\add* sent¦139314 some spies¦139316 and¦139317 knew¦139317 that Sha'ul¦139321 had definitely \add ≈arrived\add*.)
\v 5 \add That night,\add* David¦139327 \add ≈moved out\add* and¦139326 \add ≈got\add* to the place where Sha'ul had camped. \add *He\add* \add ≈could see where Sha'ul was sleeping\add*, along with Ner's¦139350 son Abner¦139347, his army commander¦139351. Sha'ul was \add ≈asleep in¦139356 the secure centre\add* with his \add ≈warriors\add* all around¦139359 him.
\p
\v 6 David¦139363 spoke to Ahimelek (the Hittite¦139369) and¦139362 to Abishai¦139372 (son of Yoab's¦139377 brother¦139376 Tseruiah¦139375) \add ≈asking\add*, “Who'll go into the camp¦139388 with me to Sha'ul¦139385?”
\p Abishai \add ≈answered¦139362\add*, “I will. I'll¦139392 go with you.”
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So¦139395 that night¦139402\add* David¦139396 and Abishai¦139397 \add ≈crept into the camp¦139407\add*. Sha'ul¦139404 was asleep \add ≈there in the centre\add* with¦139407 his spear¦139408 stuck into the ground near his head¦139412, and Abner¦139414 and \add ≈others\add* were lying \add in a circle\add* around¦139417 him¦139417.
\v 8 Abishai¦139422 \add ≈whispered\add* to David¦139425, “Today God¦139427 has \add ≈arranged for you to defeat\add* your enemy¦139431. \add ≈So\add* please¦139435 let me pierce him now with¦139432 the spear¦139436 \add ≈through him and\add* into the ground¦139437. \add ≈Only one strike will do it\add*—I won't¦139440 have to \add ≈strike him a second time¦139438\add*.
\p
\v 9 “Don't¦139449 \add ≈kill¦139451\add* him¦139451,” David¦139445 \add ≈responded¦139444\add*, “because¦139452 who \add ≈can attack\add* Yahweh's¦139457 anointed¦139456 \add ≈king\add* and¦139444 \add ≈be considered\add* innocent?”
\v 10 As Yahweh¦139465 lives, he will certainly strike¦139470 him, or \add else\add* his \add ≈time\add* will come¦139474 and he'll die¦139475, or \add maybe\add* he'll go¦139478 into battle¦139477 and be swept away.
\v 11 \add ≈May\add* Yahweh \add ≈prevent me from harming\add* Yahweh's¦139483 anointed¦139486 one.\x + \xo 26:11: \xt 1Sam 24:6.\x* \add ≈Just grab\add* the spear¦139494 that's by his head¦139496, and the jug of water¦139501, then \add ≈we can get out of here\add*.”
\v 12 \add ≈So¦139505\add* David¦139506 took¦139505 the spear¦139509 and water¦139513 jug that were near Sha'ul's head¦139514 and then¦139505 \add ≈got out of there\add*. No one saw¦139519 them, and no one woke up or realised¦139519, because¦139524 Yahweh¦139529 had \add ≈caused them all to fall into\add* a deep sleep¦139526.
\p
\v 13 Then¦139533 David¦139534 \add ≈crossed the valley\add* and¦139536 stood¦139536 on the top of the \add opposite\add* hill—\add ≈quite a distance¦139542 away\add*
\v 14 and called out to Abner and \add ≈the camp\add*, “Won't you answer¦139560, Abner?”
\p “Who are you that's \add ≈shouting\add* to the king¦139570?” Abner¦139554 answered¦139562.
\p
\v 15 “Aren't you a \add ≈warrior\add*?” David¦139574 \add ≈called out\add*. “And who in¦139584 Yisrael¦139584 is \add ≈as good as\add* you? But¦139573 why didn't¦139578 you watch over your master the king? Because one of the people¦139596 came to destroy¦139597 the king your master.
\v 16 \add ≈Your performance\add* wasn't good¦139605. As Yahweh lives, all of you¦139609 who \add ≈were supposed to be\add* watching¦139621 over your master¦139624, over Yahweh's¦139612 anointed¦139627 one, \add ≈deserve to be executed\add*. \add ≈Look around,\add* where's¦139632 the king's spear¦139634 and water¦139639 jug that¦139608 were \add ≈by\add* his head¦139641?”
\p
\v 17 Then¦139644 Sha'ul¦139645 recognised¦139644 David's¦139649 voice and¦139644 \add ≈called back\add*, “Is that your voice, my son David?”
\p “\add Yes,\add* it is my voice, my master¦139658 the king¦139659.” David¦139649 \add ≈replied\add*.
\v 18 Then¦139661 he asked, “Why is my master¦139664 chasing¦139665 his servant¦139667? What have I done¦139670? \add ≈What wrong am I guilty of\add*?
\v 19 Now please¦139679 listen¦139677, my master¦139680 the king¦139681, to your servant's¦139684 words¦139683. If it's Yahweh who's incited¦139688 you against¦139689 me, may he \add ≈accept\add* an offering¦139691, but if it's \add ≈people\add*, may they be cursed¦139696 \add ≈in front¦139698\add* of Yahweh because they've driven¦139702 me away from \add ≈enjoying Yahweh's¦139687 inheritance¦139705 for me\add*,\f + \fr 26:19 \ft This is possibly referring to David not being able to enjoy his piece of land, but we haven't said that in the translation because it's not certain. (It could be referring to having a peaceful or prosperous life, for example.)\f* saying, ‘Go \add away and¦139676\add* serve¦139709 other¦139711 gods¦139710.’
\v 20 \add ≈So¦139713\add* now, don't¦139714 let \add ≈me die far\add* from Yahweh's¦139721 \add ≈presence¦139720\add*. \add It seems that\add* Yisrael's¦139726 king¦139725 has come¦139724 \add all this way\add* to chase a flea, just like someone¦139733 chases a \add ≈wild bird\add* in¦139735 the hills.”
\p
\v 21 Sha'ul¦139738 \add ≈responded¦139737\add*, “\add Yes,\add* I've sinned¦139739. \add ≈Go home\add*, my son David¦139743. I won't¦139745 \add ≈wrong\add* you again¦139749, because¦139750 \add ≈you spared my life¦139753 today\add*. \add ≈Yes\add*, I've acted foolishly¦139758 and¦139759 \add ≈been following the wrong path\add*.”
\p
\v 22 “Look, \add ≈here's your\add* spear.” David¦139764 \add ≈called back\add*. “Get one of \add &your\add* young¦139772 men¦139772 \add ≈to come¦139770 across\add* and¦139763 get it.
\v 23 May Yahweh \add ≈repay each person for their obedience\add* and¦139775 faithfulness¦139783. Yahweh \add ≈put you¦139785 in¦139790 a vulnerable position\add* today, but¦139775 I wasn't willing¦139792 to \add ≈hurt\add* Yahweh's¦139775 anointed¦139795 \add king\add*.
\v 24 Just as \add ≈I honoured\add* your life today, so \add to\add* may Yahweh¦139809 \add ≈honour\add* my life and¦139798 rescue¦139810 me from all \add ≈my difficulties\add*.
\p
\v 25 “May you be blessed¦139821, my son David,” Sha'ul told David. “You certainly \add ≈have both ability and the skill to use it\add*.”
\p Then David¦139820 went on his way¦139833 and Sha'ul \add ≈went back home\add*.
\c 27
\s1 David among the Philistines
